{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You shall not oppress a hired servant.</b> But is it not already written? Rather, to transgress concerning the poor person with two prohibitions — ״לֹא תַעֲשֹׁק שְׂכַר שָׂכִיר״, for he is poor and needy; and concerning the rich person he was already warned (Leviticus 19) ״לֹא תַעֲשֹׁק אֶת רֵעֲךָ״ (Bava Metzia 111a):" "<b>Needy.</b> One who longs for everything." "<b>From your midst.</b> This is a ger tzedek." "<b>In your gates.</b> This is a ger toshav who eats nevelot." "<b>Who is in your land.</b> To include the hire of an animal and vessels (Bava Metzia 111a)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:14.578055217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}